# Recommended Priorities

Based on the assessment findings, the following priorities are recommended for the Documentation Improvement Project.

## High Priority

- Improve the Landing Page messaging and portfolio introduction.
- Strengthen the Documentation Homepage to better orient first-time visitors.
- Improve navigation between related documentation pages.

## Medium Priority

- Expand contextual information within Quick Start Guides.
- Enhance procedural explanations and supporting visuals.
- Improve API Reference cross-linking and developer guidance.
- Strengthen professional messaging on the Contact Page.

## Low Priority

- Continue expanding the technical blog with new articles.
- Add additional examples and supporting resources where appropriate.
- Refine portfolio polish and consistency throughout the site.

---

# Conclusion

The documentation portfolio demonstrates a solid understanding of technical writing principles and provides a strong foundation for continued improvement. The assessment identified opportunities to enhance clarity, navigation, and user guidance without requiring significant structural changes.

The findings documented in this report will guide the implementation phases of the Documentation Improvement Project. Addressing the identified priorities will strengthen the portfolio's effectiveness while further demonstrating technical writing best practices and professional documentation skills.